            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="CAR01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName>Sir</roleName>
                        <forename>Anthony</forename>
                        <surname>Carlisle</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1768-02-15">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1840-11-02"/>
                    <occupation>surgeon</occupation>
                    <occupation>anatomist</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Carlisle was appointed surgeon to the Westminster Hospital in 1793 where he later offered lectures on surgery. He was elected a fellow of the Royal Society 
      in 1804 and became professor of anatomy at the Royal Academy in 1808. Godwin met Carlisle first in 1795 and attended many of 
      his lectures in late 1796. A long-lasting friendship began which petered out only by 1814. His half-brother, <persName key="CAR04">Nicholas Carlisle,</persName> 
      was an antiquary who Godwin met in 1829. </p>
                        <p>Carlisle is listed in the 1796 lists under 1795, which accords with his entrance into the diary.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="MS"> MS. Abinger c. 17, fol. 53: 15 September 1797</bibl>
                    <bibl type="MS"> MS. Abinger c. 55, fols. 46-8: 19 September 1797</bibl>
